    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d528-a2">

                <pb facs="1137" n="1041" xml:id="pg1041"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 96.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr.
                            Garcia.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 15,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your polite note in character of secretary-general of the general-in-chief of
                    the army of date yesterday, in which you communicate to me the statement that
                    the Citizen-General Gregorio Cedeño, general-in-chief of the army of liberation
                    took possession of the capital of the republic the day preceding at the head of
                    his numerous army, after having vanquished the armed resistance which the
                    government, emanating from the convention, opposed to it, &amp;c.</p>
                <p>I shall, at the earliest opportunity, bring to the knowledge of my government the
                    state of affairs which is the subject of your note.</p>
                <p>Meantime, I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JEHU BAKER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
